From aefd065f5f511dc385a067183e5981a51fd33ae1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] version: Reaper_v3.4.3

Three fixes since v3.4.2: the kernel linearizes a non-GSO skb with more
than four page frags before the Runner drops it (IPv6 DNS-over-TLS through
a 6in4 tunnel, GT-BE98 field), the radio readers are stopped before every
rc path that tears the radios down (the wl1 + wl2 dongle traps on a
restart_net with Dynamic puncturing on, owner box), and Diagnostics
v1.3.38 reports both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 0813f08ea9..2b1c3ee614 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v3.4.2
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v3.4.3
 
 RCNO=0
-- 
2.25.1

